# P66 on Windows: withAnimation produces intermediate values.
# Nothing is pressed: the app reads itself out. Run on 2026-10-19 with Swift 6.4.0, display at 125%, both Windows backends (TEST_BACKEND=WinUI and TEST_BACKEND=gtk4); rc=0 and the replay line on all.
# Pass: SAMPLES in the tens over about 0.5 s, monotonic (macOS: 31-32 on AppKit, 26 on GTK).
# RE-TEST: WinUI read SAMPLES 3 over 0.77 s and GTK SAMPLES 2 over 1.92 s, both monotonic, but
# measured while three builds ran; not yet called a pass or a defect.
# Re-measured idle the same day: still 2 on both, so a real defect. The main dispatch queue was drained only by a poll (WinUI's SetTimer re-armed on every message; GTK's 50 ms g_timeout). Fixed by watching libdispatch's main-queue handle: WinUI 26-27 samples idle (20 under a build), GTK 7 -- GTK's remaining gap is not yet explained. 閒置重測仍是 2,修正後 WinUI 26-27、GTK 7。
